// TEST: Idx Card Non Enumerable Field (rejects)
// ============================================================================
// The v1 fence: every field must be `Int` with static bounds. A `Float` field
// has no enumeration — the solution set would not be finite, let alone
// countable by box iteration — so the struct is refused rather than silently
// enumerated over some invented discretization:
//
//   struct Mixed, field 'w': non-enumerable field type Float — an
//   index-eligible struct needs every field Int with static bounds
//
// The refusal names the FIELD, not just the struct, because a record with
// several fields gives no clue otherwise which one is the problem.
//
// Worth stating explicitly since it looks like an omission: this is a v1
// eligibility boundary, not a claim that non-Int index types are impossible.
// Sum-type fields (a `Parity` variant, the natural companion to these m-values)
// are a NAMED deferral of the plan (§8.2) blocked on StaticValue having no
// variant case; int parity is the shipped ops' own convention meanwhile, and
// index-types/147 uses it that way.
// ============================================================================
static struct Mixed {
    m: Int<min=-1, max=1>,
    w: Float
} where m + m == 0

let static CARD = idx_card(Mixed)
